.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt VPN-STATUS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vpn-status
.Nd list the VPN tunnels that are up, one word each
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl p
.Nm
.Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints, on one line, a label for each VPN tunnel that is up, separated
by spaces; the line is empty when none is.
A tunnel is a WireGuard, tun or tap interface that is both up and
running.
On
.Fx
the candidates are the interfaces of the
.Ql wg ,
.Ql tun ,
.Ql tap
and
.Ql vpn
interface groups, as
.Xr ifconfig 8
reports them; on Linux, every interface sysfs says is a WireGuard one,
or that has
.Pa tun_flags .
.Pp
A tunnel's label is the first that exists of:
.Bl -enum -offset indent
.It
the first word of its description: the
.Va ifconfig_ Ns Ar IF Ns Va _descr
of
.Xr rc.conf 5
on
.Fx ,
the interface alias on Linux
.Pq Ic ip link set Ar IF Ic alias Ar ... ;
.It
for a tun or tap interface,
.Xr openconnect 8 Ns 's
.Fl -authgroup
on the command line of the process holding it,
else that process's first argument that is not an option (the server),
else its name;
.It
for a WireGuard interface, the endpoint address of the first peer that
has one, without its port;
.It
the interface name.
.El
.Pp
A tunnel outside the default FIB on
.Fx ,
or enslaved to a VRF on Linux, has
.Ql / Ns Ar FIB
or
.Ql / Ns Ar VRF
appended:
.Ql mullvad/1 .
.Pp
A WireGuard tunnel with a
.Ql PersistentKeepalive
peer is dead when no peer has handshaken in the last three minutes plus
that keepalive interval: configured, but nothing answers.
Its label gets a trailing
.Ql \&!
.Pq Ql mullvad/1\&! .
A peer carrying traffic re-handshakes every two minutes, and keepalive
sends traffic at least once per interval.
A tunnel with no keepalive peer is not marked: when idle, its peers stop
handshaking, and that silence cannot be told from a peer that is gone.
Nor is a tunnel
.Xr wg 8
cannot be asked about, as on Linux for any user but root.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h
Print the usage and exit.
.It Fl p
Format for polybar: a dead tunnel is shown in red rather than with a
.Ql \&! ,
and no tunnel at all as a red
.Ql none .
The red is
.Ev VPN_STATUS_RED ,
else the
.Va red
that polybar's colour script
.Ev VPN_STATUS_COLORS
defines, else
.Ql #dc322f .
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width VPN_STATUS_COLORS
.It Ev PROCFS
The root of procfs on Linux, instead of
.Pa /proc ,
where the owner of a tun or tap interface is looked for.
.It Ev SYSFS
The root of sysfs on Linux, instead of
.Pa /sys .
.It Ev VPN_STATUS_COLORS
The shell script, sourced, that sets
.Va red
for
.Fl p ,
instead of
.Pa ~/.config/polybar/scripts/colors.sh .
.It Ev VPN_STATUS_RED
The colour of
.Fl p ,
outright.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
The list was printed, empty or not.
.It 1
The platform is neither
.Fx
nor Linux.
.It 2
A usage error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Two tunnels, one in FIB 1 that no longer answers:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ vpn-status
work mullvad/1!
.Ed
.Pp
A polybar module:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[module/vpn]
type = custom/script
exec = vpn-status -p
interval = 10
.Ed
.Pp
Label a
.Fx
WireGuard tunnel in
.Xr rc.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ifconfig_wg0_descr="mullvad (External VPN)"
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
.Xr ip 8 ,
.Xr wg 8
.Sh CAVEATS
A WireGuard tunnel without
.Ql PersistentKeepalive
is never marked dead, even when its peer is gone: idle, it stops
handshaking, and that silence looks the same.
Set
.Ql PersistentKeepalive
on a peer for the mark to mean something.
.Pp
On Linux two things need root:
.Xr wg 8
answers only root, so a dead WireGuard tunnel is not marked, and the
owner of a tun device run by root cannot be seen, so the tunnel is
labelled by its name.
